        {"unit_id": "u-e9cdca141412a92154b2", "start_line": 169, "end_line": 179, "role": "dependency", "dependency_reason": "The target reaches png_read_end after row reading."}
      ],
      "absence_claim": false,
      "audited_unit_ids": []
    },
    {
      "topic": "trigger",
      "statement": "png_read_update_info initializes rows when PNG_FLAG_ROW_INIT is clear. A later png_start_read_image call with that flag set takes the duplicate-call png_app_error path. The harness calls the two functions in that order.",
      "evidence": [
        {"unit_id": "u-cc1e0b2b98d159b17936", "start_line": 265, "end_line": 289, "role": "primary", "dependency_reason": ""},
        {"unit_id": "u-cc1e0b2b98d159b17936", "start_line": 297, "end_line": 312, "role": "primary", "dependency_reason": ""},
        {"unit_id": "u-e9cdca141412a92154b2", "start_line": 139, "end_line": 141, "role": "dependency", "dependency_reason": "The target calls png_read_update_info first."},
        {"unit_id": "u-e9cdca141412a92154b2", "start_line": 169, "end_line": 170, "role": "dependency", "dependency_reason": "The target later calls png_start_read_image."}
      ],
      "absence_claim": false,
      "audited_unit_ids": []
    },
    {
      "topic": "counterevidence",
      "statement": "Both versions of pngread.c supplied here have identical complete-unit hashes, so the duplicate-call contract shown in this continuation is unchanged across those versions. This fact alone does not establish the effect of png_app_error under the supplied build.",
      "evidence": [
        {"unit_id": "u-4a3ce9d69b27b864372c", "start_line": 265, "end_line": 312, "role": "primary", "dependency_reason": ""},
        {"unit_id": "u-cc1e0b2b98d159b17936", "start_line": 265, "end_line": 312, "role": "primary", "dependency_reason": ""}
      ],
      "absence_claim": false,
      "audited_unit_ids": []
    },
    {
      "topic": "trigger",
      "statement": "After updating info, the harness checks png_get_IHDR and returns on failure; it also returns when width times height exceeds its 100000000 threshold.",
